Framebuffer discard (BGFX_CLEAR_DISCARD_*) on GL, three bugs that made it never work on a phone:
- setFrameBuffer applied, when leaving a framebuffer, the flags stored when it was entered (the view before its
  first view): one framebuffer late. Now the flags of the view just finished, the last one drawn into it.
- FrameBufferGL::discard invalidated whatever framebuffer was bound (after an MSAA resolve: the back buffer); it now
  binds its own fbo[0] (for MSAA the multisampled attachments, already resolved into fbo[1]).
- On GLES depth together with stencil matched no branch; GL_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT exists in GLES 3.
The engine sets the flags only on views after which the attachments are not read again (shim scene_complete).

